        "first_page": "                                         NOTICE OF GENERAL ELECTION\nNotice is hereby given that an Election will be held on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, at the usual polling places in the\nprecincts of Washington County, Nebraska, an election will be held. The polls will be open at 8:00 o’clock a.m. and\nclose at 8:00 o’clock p.m. Said election will be for the nomination of candidates to various offices and voting on\nvarious issues. Length of term in office is 4 years unless otherwise stated.\n\n                                              UNITED STATES SENATORIAL TICKET\nUnited States Senator - Six Year Term, Vote for ONE\nRepublican      Legal Marijuana NOW          Nebraska Working People     America First         By Petition\nPete Ricketts   Mike Marvin                  Robin Richards              Chuck Conboy          Dan Osborn\n\n                                                    CONGRESSIONAL TICKET\nRepresentative in Congress, District 3 - Two Year Term, Vote for ONE\nRepublican          Democratic             Legal Marijuana NOW       Nebraska Working People           By Petition\nAdrian Smith        Becky Kelly Stille     David J. Else             Macey Budke                       Mark Cohen\n\n                                                      STATE TICKET\nGovernor and Lt Governor- Vote for ONE\nRepublican               Democratic                     Legal Marijuana NOW              America First\nJim Pillen and Joe Kelly Lynne Walz and Ben Steffen     Rick Beard and Keenya Barnes     Brett Lindstrom and Michael Picard\n\nSecretary of State – Vote for ONE\nRepublican              Democratic            Nebraska Working People              America First\nScott Petersen          Sarah J. Slattery     Paul Rumbaugh                        Bob Krist\nState Treasurer – Vote for ONE\nRepublican              Democratic\nJoey Spellerberg        Daniel Ebers\nAttorney General – Vote for ONE\nRepublican              Democratic\nMike Hilgers            Jocelyn Brasher\nAuditor of Public Accounts – Vote for ONE\nRepublican              America First\nMike Foley              John Knight\n\n                                                      COUNTY TICKET\nCounty Assessor – Vote for ONE\nRepublican\nRobin Andreasen\nCounty Attorney – Vote for ONE\nRepublican\nM. Scott Vander Schaaf\nCounty Clerk – Vote for ONE\nRepublican\nBarbara Sullivan\nClerk of District Court – Vote for ONE\nRepublican\nAmber R. Dean\nRegister of Deeds – Vote for ONE\nRepublican\nArron W. Hoden\n"
      },
